course: dictionary
lesson: 2429
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. Dab is one of these words. «Mum dabs her eyes saying "happy tears".» Here dab is a verb: she touches her eyes lightly and quickly with something soft, not rubbing hard.
explain: Look at the words next to dab to find its meaning. «Scientists dabbed that smell on living ants» means they put a small amount of smell on the ants with light touches. The words on and smell are your clues.
explain: Dab can also be a noun, meaning a small amount, as in «a dab of glue». Check by swapping in another word: «a small amount of glue» still makes sense, so dab means a small amount here. Try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Dab can be a verb, a noun, or part of a phrase, so always check the context.
fact: As a verb, dab means to touch something lightly and quickly several times, often with a cloth or sponge.
fact: As a noun, «a dab of» means a small amount of something, such as «a dab of butter».
fact: «A dab hand at» is UK informal for being very good at something.
fact: A dab is also a small flat sea fish, as in «the crab and the dab».
exercise: Mum dabs her eyes saying "happy tears". What does dabs mean here? | Pulls hard on | Shouts loudly | *Touches lightly and quickly with a cloth | Closes tightly
exercise: Sam says, "She is a dab hand at chess." What does dab hand mean? | *Very good at something | Tired and sleepy | A quick wave | A small flat sea fish
exercise: «Add a dab of butter to the pan.» What does a dab of mean? | A loud noise | *A small amount | A long pause | A large bowl
test: «The artist dabbed paint on the paper with a sponge.» What does dabbed mean here? | Washed the paper clean | Threw paint hard at the wall | *Put on a small amount with light touches | Painted a whole wall in one go
test: «The Whale ate the starfish and the garfish, and the crab and the dab.» In this sentence, what is a dab? | A kind of seaweed | A deep rock on the seabed | A big whale | *A small flat sea fish
exam: «She gave his arm a quick dab.» Which meaning of dab fits best? | A big splash | *A light, quick touch | A dance move | A small flat sea fish
